Package: MetaQCAT
Title: Meta-Analysis of Microbiome Composition Associations
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Shuren", "He", , email = "heshuren987@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fixed- and random-effect meta-analysis of microbiome composition
    and observed-zero associations using covariate-adjusted study-level score
    summaries and a null-imposed wild-score bootstrap. Independent subjects
    are the multiplier units, including for repeated observations. Null fits,
    covariance estimates and eligibility decisions remain fixed across draws.
    The random-effect composition test uses a contrast-space-induced kernel
    to obtain reference-taxon-invariant inference for eligible taxa when
    the required covariance matrices are positive definite. Methods build
    on Kline and Santos (2012) <doi:10.1515/2156-6674.1006>,
    Hemerik et al. (2020) <doi:10.1111/rssb.12369>, Tang et al. (2017)
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw804> and Lee et al. (2013)
    <doi:10.1016/j.ajhg.2013.05.010>.
